{"content":[{"c":["GESHEM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Arab opponent of Nehemiah who derided those seeking to rebuild the walls of Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.2.19","r":"Neh.2.19","rawR":"Neh.2.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.2.19","value":"Neh.2.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 2:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.6.1-6","r":"Neh.6.1-6","rawR":"Neh.6.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.6.1-6","value":"Neh.6.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:1-6"},"). He was likely an inhabitant of the north Arabian Desert and has been identified with Gashmu son of Shahr in a Dedanite Arabian inscription. Like Sanballat and Tobiah, his economic interests were threatened by the rebuilding of Jerusalem."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Geshem","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 2:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.2.19","rawQueryValue":"Neh.2.19","sourceRefExact":"Neh.2.19"},{"anchorText":"6:1-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.6.1-6","rawQueryValue":"Neh.6.1-6","sourceRefExact":"Neh.6.1-6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"624f7c9f4841979ea3d757246af810aa9e3aac7d57a64a63eb40f76b48c738e3","sourceItemName":"Geshem","sourceItemOrder":109,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Geshem","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Geshem","title":"Geshem","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}